# Fetch cache — large, regenerable, and machine-local. Deleting it only makes
# the next run slower, never wrong.
.cache/

# Extracted Catalogs. Regenerable, but keeping them out of git avoids
# committing a snapshot of 559 institutions' course listings.
catalogs/

# Run state and URL history. Regenerable from a run, and machine-local; the
# CSVs are the shareable deliverable.
pipeline.db
pipeline.db-wal
pipeline.db-shm
# Snapshots taken before a migration or repair (`.bak`, `.pre-dedupe`, ...).
# Machine-local recovery copies, like the database itself.
pipeline.db.*
pipeline.db-*

# Per-run logs: <run_id>.jsonl (structured) and <run_id>.log (readable).
logs/

# Stray console redirects. run.py writes its own readable log into logs/, but a
# launch command may still redirect stdout somewhere, and stage1.log landed in
# the repo root untracked and unignored.
*.log

# Every generated artefact, exhaustively -- 87 per-chunk files once accumulated
# in the repo root, which buried the one CSV this repo actually tracks. A new
# output kind therefore needs no new entry here.
#
# The star is load-bearing: `out/` would exclude the *directory*, and git does
# not descend into an excluded directory, so the negation below would silently
# do nothing. `out/*` excludes the contents individually, which is what makes a
# single file re-includable. Restoring the bare `out/` breaks the tracking with
# no error to show you.
out/*

# The one exception, and the only expensive artefact here: hours of crawling to
# regenerate, where everything else under out/ is disposable or takes seconds.
# 22.5MB on disk, ~3.1MB per committed revision. Commit it at milestones, not
# after every run.
!out/courses_filled.csv

# Named for documentation rather than effect -- `out/*` above matches this as a
# directory already.
# The convention: `out/` holds deliverables, `out/scratch/` holds verification
# runs, which produce files indistinguishable in shape from real output. Pass
# `--out-dir out/scratch` for anything disposable, so the directory can be
# emptied without reading filenames. See the Outputs section of README.md.
out/scratch/

# Chunk inputs. Regenerable from the sheet with tools/split_by_site.py;
# tracking them would guarantee they go stale.
chunks/
catalogs.baseline/
*.csv.bak

# Legacy output locations, kept so a checkout predating out/ stays clean.
#
# Anchored with a leading `/` because these mean "in the repo root" and a
# pattern without a slash matches at every depth: unanchored,
# `courses_filled.csv` also matched `out/courses_filled.csv` and quietly
# defeated the negation above. Nothing is lost by anchoring -- `out/*` already
# covers every direct child of out/.
/courses_filled.csv
/courses_filled.*.csv
/review_queue.csv
/review_queue.*.csv
/coverage_report.md
/coverage_report.*.md
/calibration_sample.csv
/calibration_sample.*.csv
/phase2*.csv

# Local secrets. The API key must never be committed, and broad staging in
# this repo is not hypothetical -- eaabf6f swept in 30MB of stray files.
# `.env.example` is the committed template; the real file never is.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.~lock.*
